Native Amiga blitter ownership regression
========================================

Build with test-graphics-blitterregisters or its -quick target. The native
Amiga graphics test group selects both; other targets do not select this test.

The test keeps a blitter size and source/destination pointers in D0/D1/A0/A1
across OwnBlitter and DisownBlitter. Classic Amiga callers use those registers
after the ownership calls. An unchanged ROM overwrites D0 on both calls and
clears A1 in OwnBlitter; the test reports failures without issuing an unsafe
blit using the damaged size.

When the registers are preserved, it copies 17 one-word rows between Chip RAM
buffers and checks all copied bytes and the surrounding guards. This exercises
the dimensions/pointers as hardware inputs, rather than checking wrapper code.

Expected result: BLITTER REGISTERS TEST: 0 failures.

